    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d503">

                <pb facs="0953" n="829" xml:id="pg829"/>

                <head>No. 499.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Blaine to Señor de
                    Zamacona.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1881-04-28"><hi rendition="#italic">April</hi> 28,
                        1881</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to my note of the 19th instant in
                    reply to yours of the 13th relative to the depredations upon citizens of Mexico
                    by outlaws, presumed to have their lurking place in Arizona Territory, I have
                    now the honor and the pleasure to inform you that the Secretary of the Interior
                    advises me that he has requested, by his letter of the 21st instant, the
                    governor of that Territory to exert all means within his power to suppress such
                    disturbances and to maintain quiet on the frontier.</p>
                <p>Accept, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>JAMES G. BLAINE.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
